PRIVATE STATIC GNU LIGHTNING WHOLE-PRODUCT RELINK COMPANION

PRIVATE ONLY. R1 HOLD. This kit contains compiled application material. It does
not grant or establish permission to distribute the GAME-derived application,
application objects, library sources, Windows mman shim, or any other material.
No inferred MIT grant, EULA exception, or source/object redistribution clearance.
Retain the independently reviewed rights/terms before any proposed conveyance.
The GNU lightning use/modified-source notices and GPL/LGPL texts are retained
under library/lightning. Exact win32/mman ancestry, files and README declaration
are retained separately; the complete applicable notice/grant disposition is
unresolved, not replaced by the RSP project's MIT copyright holders.

WHAT THIS KIT DOES
The actual 35mmisle link, not a synthetic application, supplied every ordered
object/archive/resource/library argument. Nested @ response files were expanded
while they existed; their original byte hashes are in kit-manifest.json. CMake
File API checks actual configuration, target closure and product object/resource
presence. Its optional commandFragments are NOT used as the final link recipe.
The Windows route preserves /MANIFEST:NO and the actual compiled .res. The Linux
route retains ordered linker flags/groups/repeated libraries and uses an
executable-relative Runtime DSO directory. No old executable is copied into the
kit or used as relink output. Only the GNU lightning archive slot is replaced.

Linux capture additionally resolves the complete recursive DT_NEEDED graph with
the native CMake file(GET_RUNTIME_DEPENDENCIES) ELF/objdump resolver, following
RPATH/RUNPATH and ldconfig, then the bounded parent directories of explicit DSO
link inputs for extracted SDK siblings. --trace alone is NOT a runtime closure.
Unresolved names, conflicting SONAME identities or missing
captured dependencies reject the kit. Every non-system original is hash-bound
at capture and copied with relative kit paths and required SONAME aliases;
external System Library identities and dependency edges are recorded separately.
Original private RPATH/RUNPATH strings stay in private capture only; the kit
records their hashes, not producer directories. Recipient staging rewrites only
DSO copies and supplies both executable-relative runtime lookup and a separate
relative runtime-directory link-time search path.

The kit has exact prepared lightning source, all headers/backends/support/build
inputs, win32/mman, source/patch hashes, retained upstream archive identity,
preparation scripts/tool hashes, actual standalone compilation flags, real
non-lightning application link inputs, ordered recipe, and toolchain/config/CRT
receipt. No GAME source, ROM, save/profile, producer build tree or toolchain/SDK
binaries are included. Source modification intentionally does not invoke the
producer's source preparation/rematerialization script.
The exact pinned upstream mman/sys/.vs/mman/v14/.suo is personal IDE state, not
source or build control. Its identity is in library/provenance/excluded-upstream-ide-cache.json.
Only that cache is omitted; all source and compilation/installation controls remain included.

PREREQUISITES AND LIMITS
Use the recorded native x64 platform and @CONFIGURATION@ configuration.
Install the exact compiler/linker components and matching System Libraries
identified by basename/SHA-256 in kit-manifest.json. relink verifies them before
calling the actual linker. Windows requires VS2022/MSVC x64 native developer
shell, the recorded toolset/Windows SDK, and /MT (/MTd for Debug). Linux requires
the recorded native compiler/binutils, Python 3, CMake >=3.24, Ninja, readelf and
patchelf. readelf is producer-side metadata inspection; patchelf changes ONLY
recipient-staged DSO copies to $ORIGIN, not kit inputs or SDK originals.
These are ordinary native objects: detected GCC/LLVM/MSVC LTO-only material and
thin archives reject kit creation, without changing the producer's flags.
This is not a generic compiler/ABI portability claim. Compiler debug records in
opaque PRIVATE objects have not been promised redacted; separately review their
privacy before any distribution. Text metadata/recipes contain no producer paths.

Capture and recipient relink both reject LINK/_LINK_ implicit options before
invoking tools. Linux also rejects ambient GCC_EXEC_PREFIX, COMPILER_PATH,
LIBRARY_PATH, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, LD_RUN_PATH and LD_PRELOAD. Use a clean recorded
native toolchain environment, not hidden search/injection overrides. Windows
still requires the real developer LIB environment, whose selected System Library
files must match the captured hashes.

Linux --push-state/--pop-state preserve the library-selection stack, including
restoring static/dynamic selection before resolving later -l arguments.
Alternate driver linker/toolchain selectors (-fuse-ld, --ld-path, -B prefixes,
specs/wrapper/toolchain/target overrides) are explicitly rejected. Capture asks
the native driver for its default linker, requires agreement with CMake's
linker, and fingerprints that resolved tool. Recipient relink repeats the driver
query and verifies that actual default-linker hash; it does not check an unused
linker selected only by an old producer path.

Use an independently extracted copy in a spaces/non-ASCII path and make the
producer source/build directories unavailable for all following link commands.
No ROM is needed to build lightning, run synthetic JIT, or relink the product.
The existing matching private Runtime bundle supplies renderer assets/notices
and Windows runtime DLLs/OS graphics/audio/device prerequisites; it is not an
application object substitute. To run the whole product, retain that bundle's
normal resources, and use a newly linked executable rather than its old binary.
Linux output additionally gets its own adjacent lib/ containing the supplied
non-system DSOs, with executable $ORIGIN/lib and DSO $ORIGIN RUNPATH. Reusing an
existing output or DSO destination is rejected rather than silently overwriting
candidate evidence. Do not sign/strip/reinstall before preserving relink evidence.

LINUX: BASELINE STANDALONE LIBRARY AND ACTUAL WHOLE PRODUCT
From the extracted kit directory, with the recorded compiler selected:
  cmake -S library -B build-lightning -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=@CONFIGURATION@
  cmake --build build-lightning --config @CONFIGURATION@
  ./build-lightning/lightning-jit-proof
  python3 runtime_relink.py relink --lightning build-lightning/libisle-rsp-lightning.a --output baseline/35mmisle

WINDOWS: BASELINE (native x64 VS2022 developer PowerShell)
  cmake -S library -B build-lightning -G "Visual Studio 17 2022" -A x64 -DCMAKE_CONFIGURATION_TYPES=@CONFIGURATION@
  cmake --build build-lightning --config @CONFIGURATION@
  & .\build-lightning\@CONFIGURATION@\lightning-jit-proof.exe
  python runtime_relink.py relink --lightning build-lightning/@CONFIGURATION@/isle-rsp-lightning.lib --output baseline/35mmisle.exe

If the compiler/linker is not on PATH, relink accepts --driver with its current
recipient path. It must still match every captured hash. No producer absolute
path or fallback to a different compiler is used.

REAL MODIFICATION AND SYNTHETIC JIT PROOF
The following command modifies the delivered library's actual init_jit body to
write @MARKER@ to stderr. This is an explicitly requested private proof
modification, never applied automatically to the producer's runtime/library.
  python3 runtime_relink.py mark-proof --library library

Linux:
  cmake -S library -B build-lightning-modified -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=@CONFIGURATION@
  cmake --build build-lightning-modified --config @CONFIGURATION@
  python3 runtime_relink.py prove --program build-lightning-modified/lightning-jit-proof --evidence modified-jit-proof.json
  python3 runtime_relink.py relink --lightning build-lightning-modified/libisle-rsp-lightning.a --output modified/35mmisle

Windows (use python rather than python3 for mark-proof as well):
  cmake -S library -B build-lightning-modified -G "Visual Studio 17 2022" -A x64 -DCMAKE_CONFIGURATION_TYPES=@CONFIGURATION@
  cmake --build build-lightning-modified --config @CONFIGURATION@
  python runtime_relink.py prove --program build-lightning-modified/@CONFIGURATION@/lightning-jit-proof.exe --evidence modified-jit-proof.json
  python runtime_relink.py relink --lightning build-lightning-modified/@CONFIGURATION@/isle-rsp-lightning.lib --output modified/35mmisle.exe

The proof program executes actual generated machine code returning 42/43 with
sequential and overlapping lightning state lifetimes. prove requires both its
real zero exit and marker in actual stderr; it never fabricates/injects that
marker into captured output. The relink receipt records the exact replacement
archive hash, output executable hash, actual response hash, and staged DSO hashes.
The product link is still the actual product's entire captured object closure,
not the proof program. Different archive hashes alone are NOT execution proof.

GENUINE PRODUCT PROOF (PARENT-OWNED; EXTERNAL ADMITTED INPUTS ONLY)
Use a separate copy of the matching Runtime resources, put the newly linked
modified executable in the normal executable location, and preserve its adjacent
Linux lib/ directory. No old executable may be used. From the extracted kit,
set ADMITTED_ROM to the independently admitted actual ROM and FRESH_PRIVATE_DATA
to a fresh private application-data directory (neither is a kit input).
Linux:
  python3 runtime_relink.py prove --program modified/35mmisle --evidence modified-product-proof.json -- "$ADMITTED_ROM" --data-directory "$FRESH_PRIVATE_DATA"
Windows PowerShell:
  python runtime_relink.py prove --program modified/35mmisle.exe --evidence modified-product-proof.json -- "$env:ADMITTED_ROM" --data-directory "$env:FRESH_PRIVATE_DATA"
Run real ordinary startup/input and close the actual window normally, preserving
its real exit. If resources need the normal Runtime layout, use --program with
the newly linked executable's location there, not the example modified directory.
--help is NOT product proof: it does not invoke the JIT. No fake input, callbacks,
profile authoring, or campaign-state manipulation is part of this companion.
A genuine library marker is necessary but not sufficient for all product gates.
Existing parent-owned RSP regression/runtime/platform checks remain required;
no Linux/Windows/gameplay/audio/campaign qualification is transferred by a link.

PRODUCER INTEGRATION (NOT A RECIPIENT BUILD REQUIREMENT)
After the final 35mmisle target/resource/install-RPATH setup in root CMake:
  include(cmake/RuntimeRelink.cmake)
  isle_add_runtime_relink_kit()
Producer configure requires CMake >=3.27 for same-generation File API queries.
Ordinary builds and this standalone recipient library retain their 3.24 minimum.
Configure the existing native preset with -DISLE_BUILD_RUNTIME_RELINK_KIT=ON,
build the actual 35mmisle, then explicitly build --target runtime-relink-kit
(--config @CONFIGURATION@ on MSBuild). The default output is the PRIVATE binary
tree's private-runtime-relink-kit/@CONFIGURATION@. ISLE_RUNTIME_RELINK_OUTPUT
can select a private destination. Existing uninstrumented products have no valid
capture: configure ON BEFORE building; force a genuine final relink if needed.
Never add this target/output to CPack Source, Runtime install, or automatic
artifact upload. Native MSVC CI must actually build and execute all above proof
routes before claiming that platform, rather than relying on Linux generation.

Capture interfaces/documentation:
  https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/prop_tgt/LANG_LINKER_LAUNCHER.html
  https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/prop_tgt/VS_GLOBAL_variable.html
  https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/msbuild/link-task?view=visualstudio
MSBuild LinkToolExe/LinkToolPath route Link's tool executable/path; the dedicated
native /MT forwarding tool preserves the original command tail and Python reads
live response inputs before forwarding to the actual recorded CMAKE_LINKER.
Check native CI's generated product project and actual wrapper capture receipt;
a missing capture fails the kit instead of substituting Unix link.txt or guessed
File API fragments. Linux adds --trace for linker-input diagnostics only.
  https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/command/file.html#get-runtime-dependencies

Publication, if independently authorized in the future, still needs complete
applicable rights/relink terms and source/kit/binary availability/access notices,
LGPL/GPL obligations, and candidate-specific composition/runtime evidence. A
private generated companion is not public corresponding-source delivery, and
this mechanism does not resolve the mman/GAME/other R1 holds.
